* CPP       117 12181   7090 I/O SUBROUTINE                             CPP 0001
*      FAP                                                              NUCPP002
*NUCPP  N.Y.U. SUBROUTINE. A FAP PROGRAM WHICH WHEN USED BY A FAP PROG. NUCPP003
*              THROUGH THE USE OF THE CALL PSEUDO-OP MAKES FORTRAN I/O  NUCPP004
*              SUBROUTINES AVAILABLE FOR READ CARD, PUNCH CARD + PRINT. NUCPP005
*              THE THREE ENTRIES ARE                                    NUCPP006
*      1. CALL NURAC,F,R1,S1,R2,S2,.....,RN,SN        (READ A CARD)     NUCPP007
*      2. CALL NUPAC,F,W1,S1,W2,S2,.....,WN,SN        (PUNCH A CARD)    NUCPP008
*      3. CALL NUPAL,F,W1,S1,W2,S2,.....,WN,SN        (PRINT A LINE)    NUCPP009
*      WHERE   F  IS THE LOCATION OF THE FORMAT  (STORED FOWARDS)       NUCPP010
*              W  ARE THE ITEMS TO BE PUNCHED OR PRINTED.               NUCPP011
*              R   ARE THE ITEMS TO BE READ FROM CARD                   NUCPP012
*              S  ARE THE SUCCESSIVE NUMBERS OF W (OR R) ITEMS AFFECTED NUCPP013
*      SPECIAL NOTE... THIS ROUTINE (WITH THE SAME ENTRY POINT NAMES) ISNUCPP014
*              ALREADY A PART OF NUSNUP, A LARGER SUB-ROUINE WHICH      NUCPP015
*              PROVIDES ENTRIES TO PERFORM ALL FORTRAN I/O OPERATIONS.  NUCPP016
       COUNT   94                                                       NUCPP017
       ENTRY   NURAC                                  (READ A CARD)     NUCPP018
       ENTRY   NUPAC                                  (PUNCH A CARD)    NUCPP019
       ENTRY   NUPAL                                  (PRINT A LINE)    NUCPP020
*      ***    IF STANDARD ERROR PROCEDURE NOT IN SYSTEM MAKE THIS A PZE NUCPP021
*      ***   AND MAKE THIS  A    BCI  1,NUCPP                           NUCPP022
*                                                                       NUCPP023
 NURAC CAL     ATSLI              A TSX (SLI),4                         NUCPP024
       SLW     TOSLR                                                    NUCPP025
       CAL     ATRTN         TSX RTN,4                                  NUCPP026
       SLW     RESTOR+1                                                 NUCPP027
       CAL     ATCSH         TSX CSH,4                                  NUCPP028
       SLW     TOCALL                                                   NUCPP029
       TRA     SAVER                                                    NUCPP030
 NUPAC CAL     ATSCH              A TSX (SCH),4                         NUCPP031
       SLW     TOCALL                                                   NUCPP032
       TRA     *+3                                                      NUCPP033
 NUPAL CAL     ATSPH              A TSX (SPH),4                         NUCPP034
       SLW     TOCALL                                                   NUCPP035
       CAL     ATSLO                                                    NUCPP036
       SLW     TOSLR                                                    NUCPP037
       CAL     ATFIL         TSX FIL,4                                  NUCPP038
       SLW     RESTOR+1                                                 NUCPP039
 SAVER SXA     SAV2,2                                                   NUCPP040
       SXA     SAV1,1                                                   NUCPP041
       AXT     SAVER,1                                                  NUCPP042
       SXD     NURAC-2,4                                                NUCPP043
       LXD     NURAC-2,2                                                NUCPP044
       CLA     ANOP         FOR INITIAL ENTRY CONDITIONS                NUCPP045
       STO     TOCALL-1                                                 NUCPP046
       CLA     1,2           LOCATION OF FORMAT STATEMENT               NUCPP047
*                                        TOOK OUT STA ONEDC             NUCPP048
*                                        TOOK OUT CLA ONEDC             NUCPP049
       STO     LCFOR                                                    NUCPP050
 TNARG CAL     2,2           ARE THERE MORE ARGUMENTS                   NUCPP051
       ARS     15                                                       NUCPP052
       LAS     ATSXZ         IS NEXT ARG. A TSX WITH A TAG OF ZERO      NUCPP053
 TREST TRA     RESTOR                                                   NUCPP054
       TRA     *+2           YES                                        NUCPP055
       TRA     RESTOR        NO                                         NUCPP056
       CLA     2,2           LOC. OF ARRAY                              NUCPP057
       ADD     AONE          ADD A ONE FOR FORTRAN ROUTINES             NUCPP058
       STA     LCARY                                                    NUCPP059
 AGAIN CAL     3,2           SHOULD CONTAIN THE SIZE OF THE ARRAY       NUCPP060
       ARS     15                                                       NUCPP061
       LAS     ATSXZ                                                    NUCPP062
       TRA     RESTOW        IF IT DOES NOT SUPPLU A SIZE ONE           NUCPP063
       TRA     *+2                                                      NUCPP064
       TRA     RESTOW                                                   NUCPP065
       CLA     3,2           SIZE OF ARRAY                              NUCPP066
 STRSZ STA     LCSZE                                                    NUCPP067
       NOP      INITIALLY=NOP, THEREAFTER A TRA TOSLR                   NUCPP068
TOCALL TSX     **,4          TO $(SCH) OR $(SPH) OR $(SCH)              NUCPP069
 LCFOR TSX     0,0,0  WILL GIVE ADDRESS OF FORMAT (STORED FOWARDS)      NUCPP070
 TOSLR TSX     **,4          TOTO $(SLI) OR $(SLO)                      NUCPP071
 LCARY PZE     **            LOC. + 1 OF ARRAY                          NUCPP072
 LCSZE PZE     **            SIZE OF ARRAY                              NUCPP073
       CLA     TTOSLR           A TRA TOSLR                             NUCPP074
       STO     TOCALL-1      IF MORE ARGUMENTS SKIP THE TSX TO CALL.PROGNUCPP075
       TXI     TNARG,2,-2    PICK UP NEXT ARGUMENTS                     NUCPP076
       REM                                                              NUCPP077
RESTOW TXI     *+1,2,1       THERE WAS NO SIZE GIVEN FOR LAST ARRAY SO  NUCPP078
       CLA     AONE          SUPPLY A SIZE OF ONE AND FIX X2 FOR RETURN NUCPP079
       TRA     STRSZ                                                    NUCPP080
       REM                                                              NUCPP081
RESTOR TXL     NOLIST,1,SAVER                                           NUCPP082
       TSX     **,4                                                     NUCPP083
       STZ     LCARY                                                    NUCPP084
 SAV1  AXT     **,1                                                     NUCPP085
       PXA     0,2                                                      NUCPP086
 SAV2  AXT     **,2                                                     NUCPP087
       PAX     0,4                                                      NUCPP088
       TRA     2,4                                                      NUCPP089
       REM                                                              NUCPP090
 AONE  PZE     1,0,0                                                    NUCPP091
*                                  TOOK OUT SYMBOLIC LOC.  ONEDC        NUCPP092
 ATSXZ OCT     0074000                                                  NUCPP093
 ATSLI TSX     $(SLI),4                                                 NUCPP094
 ATSLO TSX     $(SLO),4                                                 NUCPP095
 ATRTN TSX     $(RTN),4                                                 NUCPP096
 ATFIL TSX     $(FIL),4                                                 NUCPP097
 ATCSH TSX     $(CSH),4                                                 NUCPP098
 ATSPH TSX     $(SPH),4                                                 NUCPP099
 ATSCH TSX     $(SCH),4                                                 NUCPP100
TTOSLR TRA     TOSLR                                                    NUCPP101
ATREST TRA     RESTOR+2                                                 NUCPP102
 ANOP  NOP                                                              NUCPP103
*                                                                       NUCPP104
NOLIST TXI     *+1,1,1                                                  NUCPP105
       CAL     RESTOR+1                                                 NUCPP106
       SLW     TOSLR                                                    NUCPP107
       CAL     ATREST                                                   NUCPP108
       SLW     LCARY                                                    NUCPP109
       TRA     STRSZ+1                                                  NUCPP110
       END                                                              NUCPP111
 THE FOLLOWING TWO CARDS SHOULD BE SUBSTITUTED IN THE DECK IF ASSEMBLY *NUCPP112
  IS MADE WITH A SYSTEM WHICH DOES NOT CONTAIN THE STANDARD ERROR      *NUCPP113
 CEDURE.  THE PROGRAM STORES INDEX 4 IN THE PLACE OCCUPIED BY THE PZE. *NUCPP114
       PZE       TO BE USED IF STANDARD ERROR NOT IN SYSTEM. NUCPP021   NUCPP115
       BCI     1,NUCPP   USE IF STANDARD ERROR NOT IN SYSTEM  NUCPP022  NUCPP116
**************       LAST CARD NUCPP                                   *NUCPP117
